# venvs
backend/.venv/
frontend/.venv/

# Python cache / compiled
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Streamlit outputs
frontend/runs/
frontend/runs_uploads/
frontend/.streamlit/

# Preprocessed data
data_preprocessed/

# Local path cache
frontend/.tg_paths.json

# Daily forecast run outputs (artifacts, incl. treasury outputs — never commit).
# Note the pattern: the CONTENTS are ignored, not the directory. `backend/forecast_runs/` would
# exclude the directory itself, and git never descends into an excluded directory -- so the
# negations below would silently do nothing.
backend/forecast_runs/**
!backend/forecast_runs/
!backend/forecast_runs/*/

# ...except the two SUMMARY files. The Agent's entry point is SUMMARY.json, and with the whole
# directory ignored NO run artifact existed in a clone at all -- so a consumer could not read one,
# and the two fields it needs (data_file, client_framing) had nowhere to appear. Fields being
# correct in the writer while absent from every artifact was the blocker, not the code.
#
# Safe to track because these two are AGGREGATE ONLY: model names, MAEs, skill percentages, gate
# verdicts and the data file's NAME. No row-level predictions, no Treasury series. That is the same
# class as forecasts/published/, which is tracked for the same reason. The row-level artifacts
# (predictions_long.csv, leaderboard.csv, metrics_long.csv) stay ignored.
!backend/forecast_runs/*/SUMMARY.json
!backend/forecast_runs/*/SUMMARY.txt

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# Published forecasts ARE tracked -- forecasts/published/ is the only record of what was
# actually said, and a scorecard nobody can audit is worthless. Working forward artifacts
# under backend/forecast_runs/ stay ignored; those are regenerable, a published forecast is
# not.
!forecasts/published/
!forecasts/scorecard.csv

# ...with ONE deliberate exception: the persisted estimator blobs. This diverges from the rule
# directly above, and the reason is not disk (measured: 10.45 MB per issue). A fitted estimator
# embeds client data -- the full training target and trailing-level series, plus tree split
# thresholds and leaf values that are functions of the training data and CANNOT be scrubbed at
# all. Committing one would place raw Treasury figures permanently in every clone of a World Bank
# repository, unremovable without rewriting history.
#
# The manifest IS tracked, and carries a SHA-256 per blob. So a clone can still prove which
# estimator produced a published number and detect a substituted one; what it cannot do is run it.
# forecast.csv IS the claim and must survive a clone; an estimator only re-derives it.
# See backend/estimator_store.py.
forecasts/published/*/estimators/*
!forecasts/published/*/estimators/manifest.json

# Phase 2 experiments. The append-only log AND its per-run detail JSONs are tracked:
# verify_log_integrity() requires a JSON for every row, so ignoring runs/ would make a
# fresh clone fail its own integrity check and "reproducible from a logged run" a claim
# with nothing behind it. They are small and text.
# test_access.log is a local ledger of holdout reads -- it must not be rewritable by a
# checkout, so it stays untracked and §0a of reports/HANDOFF.md is the durable record.
experiments/test_access.log

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# LOCAL-ONLY VAULT FOR REAL CLIENT DATA AND THE REAL AUDIT TRAIL
#
# The sanitization (docs/sessions/2026-08-13-sanitize-and-synthesize.md) replaced the real
# Georgian Treasury dataset with a synthetic one so the repo carries no client data. The real
# files -- and, importantly, the REAL experiments/log.csv with its 153 genuine run records --
# are moved here rather than deleted, because the log is provenance: it is the evidence behind
# every measured claim in reports/ and docs/, and destroying it would make those claims
# unverifiable.
#
# Nothing in here may ever be committed. It is deliberately a single top-level directory so the
# rule is one line and impossible to misread.
private_vault/
data/
